{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-019-v3","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"inertia resists changes in the vase's motion, and the cloth's force is brief","working":"The vase initially at rest tends to stay at rest due to inertia. When the tablecloth is yanked quickly, it exerts a frictional force on the vase, but only for a very short time. The resulting impulse is small, so the vase's change in velocity is small and it stays nearly in place. Gravity does not prevent friction from acting, and the cloth does exert a force unless it is frictionless.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":451,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":67,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":372,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":133,"reasoningTokens":239},"totalTokens":823,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":451,"completion_tokens":372,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":67,"total_tokens":823,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":239}},"reasoningTokens":239,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4496,"keyed_label":"A"}
