{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-034-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"21000 N","working":"At the lowest point of the dip, the car experiences an upward centripetal acceleration: a_c = v^2 / R = (15 m/s)^2 / (30 m) = 225 / 30 = 7.5 m/s^2. By Newton's second law in the vertical direction (taking upward as positive): N - mg = m*a_c, which gives N = m(g + v^2/R). Substituting the given values: N = 1200 kg * (10 m/s^2 + 7.5 m/s^2) = 1200 kg * 17.5 m/s^2 = 21000 N.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":413,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":413,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":531,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":202,"reasoningTokens":329},"totalTokens":944,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":329,"promptTokenCount":413,"candidatesTokenCount":202,"totalTokenCount":944,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":413}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":202}]},"reasoningTokens":329,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4466,"keyed_label":"C"}
