{"key":"u13-apphy1-mcq-038-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"increases to 9 times its initial value","working":"The elastic potential energy stored in an ideal spring is given by U = (1/2)kx^2, where x is the displacement from the natural length (x = 0). At x_i = +0.10 m, U_i = (1/2)k(0.10)^2. At x_f = +0.30 m, U_f = (1/2)k(0.30)^2. The ratio U_f / U_i is (0.30 / 0.10)^2 = 3^2 = 9. Therefore, the elastic potential energy increases to 9 times its initial value.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":421,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":421,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":499,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":187,"reasoningTokens":312},"totalTokens":920,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":312,"promptTokenCount":421,"candidatesTokenCount":187,"totalTokenCount":920,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":421}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":187}]},"reasoningTokens":312,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4394,"keyed_label":"C"}
